This is the exercism Java zipper exercise. The Zipper class is a mutable zipper: fields are `up`, `left`, `right`, and there's probably also a `value` field (getValue()). The tests use `zipper.left.right.getValue()` and `zipper.up`, so the fields are public/package-private.

Design: Zipper holds a value, a parent (up), and left/right children. setLeft/setRight return a new Zipper (but the tests ignore the return value and use the fields directly — in fact, the tests do `zipper.setLeft(new Zipper(2)); zipper.left.setRight(new Zipper(3));` — meaning setLeft must mutate `this.left` and also return a new zipper. The standard exercism solution: setLeft mutates this.left and returns this.

Wait, but testToTree: `zipper.toTree()` equals binaryTree — so BinaryTree needs equals. And `differentPathToSameZipper` — zipper1 and zipper2 must be equal. zipper1 = root.left.up.right. If up is a shared parent reference, then root.left.up is the same Zipper object as root, so root.left.up.right is the same object as root.right → equal by identity. So Zipper doesn't need equals, but BinaryTree does (testToTree compares zipper.toTree() and binaryTree).

Standard exercism solution:

```java
class Zipper {
    int value;
    Zipper up;
    Zipper left;
    Zipper right;

    Zipper(int val) { this.value = val; }

    BinaryTree toTree() {
        Zipper root = this;
        while (root.up != null) root = root.up;
        return new BinaryTree(root);
    }

    int getValue() { return value; }

    Zipper setLeft(Zipper leftChild) {
        left = leftChild;
        if (leftChild != null) leftChild.up = this;
        return this;
    }

    Zipper setRight(Zipper rightChild) {
        right = rightChild;
        if (rightChild != null) rightChild.up = this;
        return this;
    }

    void setValue(int val) { value = val; }
}

class BinaryTree {
    Zipper root;

    BinaryTree(int value) { root = new Zipper(value); }

    BinaryTree(Zipper root) { this.root = root; }

    Zipper getRoot() { return root; }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (o == null || getClass() != o.getClass()) return false;
        BinaryTree that = (BinaryTree) o;
        return treeEquals(root, that.root);
    }

    private static boolean treeEquals(Zipper a, Zipper b) {
        if (a == null || b == null) return a == b;
        return a.value == b.value && treeEquals(a.left, b.left) && treeEquals(a.right, b.right);
    }

    String printTree() { return printTree(root); }

    private String printTree(Zipper z) {
        if (z == null) return "null";
        return "value: " + z.value + ", " +
               "left: { " + printTree(z.left) + " }, " +
               "right: { " + printTree(z.right) + " }";
    }
}
```

