So:
```java
private String print(Zipper z) {
    if (z == null) return "null";
    return "value: " + z.value + ", left: " + child(z.left) + ", right: " + child(z.right);
}
private String child(Zipper z) {
    if (z == null) return "null";
    return "{ " + print(z) + " }";
}
```

Check the expected value: `"value: 1, left: { value: 2, left: null, right: null }, right: { value: 4, left: null, right: null }"` — matches.

Also, printTree for a subtree: `"right: { value: 6, left: { value: 7, ... }, right: { value: 8, ... } }"` — nested braces work.

